This adds an option in renderpath to enable refraction.
It is complex to make it a postprocess effect, and anyway this only concerns translucent objects, so what it does is writing the desired functions and code to the translucent.frag.glsl shader of the object.
This starts with a copy of the ssr_pass, for now I just replaced the reflect() function with refract(). Parts of the code has to be removed or modified in either make_transluc.py or make_mesh.py still. But since I can't test it i'm opening the pull request already to have answers on the issue:
```
float getDeltaDepth(const vec3 hit) {
	depth = textureLod(gbufferD, getProjectedCoord(hit), 0.0).r * 2.0 - 1.0;
	vec3 viewPos = getPosView(viewRay, depth, cameraProj);
	return viewPos.z - hit.z;
}
```
calls:
```
vec3 getPosView(const vec3 viewRay, const float depth, const vec2 cameraProj) {
	float linearDepth = cameraProj.y / (cameraProj.x - depth);
	// float linearDepth = cameraProj.y / ((depth * 0.5 + 0.5) - cameraProj.x);
	return viewRay * linearDepth;
}
```
But when lunching Krom, 
```
'getPosView' : no matching overloaded function found 
'=' :  cannot convert from ' const float' to ' temp 3-component vector of float' : compilation terminated
```

This case is a follow-up of this discussion: https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/21307 

@wbamberg, @estelle and I convened of adding the mention of the universal selector being of type `type` on this page.

Here is a proposition of fix.

